   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "וְלֹא בְּקַטְלָא. מַאי קַטְלָא — מְנַקְּטָא פָּארֵי. נְזָמִים — נִזְמֵי הָאָף.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «And» a woman may «not» go out on Shabbat «with a katla.» The Gemara explains: «What is» a «katla? A» type of «small bib» hung from the neck. The «nezamim» mentioned in the mishna with which a woman may not go out on Shabbat refer to «nose rings,» not earrings."
  }
